What:          /sys/bus/platform/devices/*memory-controller/frequency
Date:          June 2026
Contact:       Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
Description:
               Current DDR PHY clock frequency in Hz. This follows the
               existing memory-controller frequency ABI. Since DDR transfers
               on both clock edges, this is half the data rate in MT/s after
               unit conversion; DDR3-1866 is reported as 933000000.
What:          /sys/bus/platform/devices/*memory-controller/dram_data_rate
Date:          June 2026
Contact:       Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
Description:
               Current DDR data rate in MT/s as one decimal integer.
What:          /sys/bus/platform/devices/*memory-controller/dram_type
Date:          June 2026
Contact:       Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
Description:
               Configured DRAM protocol name: UNKNOWN, DDR2, DDR3, DDR4,
               LPDDR2, LPDDR3, LPDDR4, or LPDDR5.
What:          /sys/bus/platform/devices/*memory-controller/channel_count
Date:          June 2026
Contact:       Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
Description:
               Number of DRAM controller channels as one decimal integer.
What:          /sys/bus/platform/devices/*memory-controller/dram_size
Date:          June 2026
Contact:       Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
Description:
               Total installed DRAM capacity in bytes, calculated from the
               controller's rank boundary and rank configuration registers.
               This is the physical controller capacity, before reserved
               memory and other kernel accounting are subtracted.
What:          /sys/bus/platform/devices/*memory-controller/mr4_ch[01]
Date:          June 2026
Contact:       Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
Description:
               Hardware-captured MR4 value for the indicated channel. The
               files are present only on controllers with hardware MR4 reads.
What:          /sys/bus/platform/devices/*memory-controller/rank_count
What:          /sys/bus/platform/devices/*memory-controller/rank_sizes
Date:          June 2026
Contact:       Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
Description:
               Optional firmware-described rank count and rank sizes in bytes.
               Rank sizes are ordered, space-separated decimal integers.
What:          /sys/bus/platform/devices/*memory-controller/mode_registers
Date:          June 2026
Contact:       Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
Description:
               Optional firmware-described mode-register values, starting at
               MR0, as ordered space-separated decimal integers.
What:          /sys/bus/platform/devices/*memory-controller/available_frequencies
Date:          June 2026
Contact:       Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
Description:
               Optional firmware-described supported DDR PHY clock
               frequencies in Hz as ordered space-separated decimal integers.
Userspace notes:
               Installed and usable system RAM is described by the device
               tree /memory node's reg property. The dram_size file is a
               controller-register diagnostic and must not replace that
               standard description.
               Static SDRAM topology should use JEDEC sdram-channel-N nodes,
               rank@N children, and the standard density and io-width
               properties. A controller supporting runtime frequency changes
               should register with devfreq, whose standard files are cur_freq
               and available_frequencies, instead of adding writable files to
               this telemetry ABI.
